Font Logos has no open licence that Nerd Fonts could name, and what it holds
is the logos of Linux distributions and other projects (U+F300 to U+F381).
Those logos are trademarks of their owners. spandeck ships them only as part
of the unchanged font, draws one only where a program in a pane prints it, and
is not affiliated with or endorsed by any of the projects.

The glyphs of Pomicons are shipped under the font's own name ("Symbols Nerd
Font Mono"), as Nerd Fonts released them; spandeck's name for the family in
its style sheet ("Spandeck Symbols") is not a name of the font file.

Fonts the owner uploads in the Appearance editor are the owner's files. They
are kept on the owner's stations and are not part of spandeck.

Colour palettes

The Control Deck's built-in themes (crates/web/assets/look.js) include these
palettes. Only the colour values are used. The deck colours shown beside each
(bars, buttons, lines) are spandeck's own choice from the same palette, and
the terminal's contrast floor set with the two Solarized themes is spandeck's.

